RAG -  RAG stands for Retrieval-Augmented Generation.

It is an AI architecture that combines the power of information retrieval with Large Language Models (LLMs) to produce more accurate and up-to-date responses.

How RAG Works:-
User asks a question
Example: "What is Snowflake Zero Copy Cloning?"
Retrieve
The system searches a knowledge source such as:
Company documents
PDFs
Databases
SharePoint
Confluence
Websites
Vector databases (Pinecone, FAISS, ChromaDB, Milvus)
Augment
The retrieved relevant information is added to the user's prompt.
Generate
The LLM (such as GPT) generates an answer based on both:
its pretrained knowledge, and
the retrieved documents.
